  "id": "processing-efficiency-theory",
  "term": "processing-efficiency theory",
  "definition": "Processing-efficiency theory is the view that anxiety can reduce the working-memory resources available for a task, which can in turn harm performance and learning. In this packet, it is used to explain how math anxiety may divert cognitive resources away from learning mathematics, especially when working-memory capacity is low.",
